{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtAbsolutelyIrreducible","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RepresentationCharacter"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.finrank_homG_specht","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.finrank_homG_specht","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtSchurDiagonal.lean#L124-L147","doc":"**The Schur pairing is orthonormal on Specht modules, over any characteristic-zero\nfield.** `dim_k Hom_G(S^μ, S^ν) = 1` if `μ = ν` and `0` otherwise.\n\nMathlib's orthonormality (`FDRep.char_orthonormal`) carries `[IsAlgClosed k]`; neither half\nof this needs it. The `1` is W2 (`SpechtAbsolutelyIrreducible.specht_end_scalar`); the `0` is\nthe classification's own Schur argument, exported above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.homG_specht_cross_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.homG_specht_cross_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtSchurDiagonal.lean#L107-L122","doc":"**Schur, off the diagonal.** For distinct diagrams of the same size there is no nonzero\nequivariant map `S^μ → S^ν`.\n\nBoth simplicity hypotheses come from `SpechtClassification.spechtRep_stable_eq_bot_or_top`;\non the `ν` side, stability under every `spechtRepOn h g` is the same condition as stability\nunder every `spechtRep ν σ`, because `transportPermHom h` is surjective. The\nnon-isomorphism is `specht_pairwise_noniso`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.finrank_homG_specht_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.finrank_homG_specht_self","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtSchurDiagonal.lean#L80-L98","doc":"**The Schur diagonal is exactly 1, over any characteristic-zero field.**\n`dim_k Hom_G(S^μ, S^μ) = 1`.\n\n`one_le_finrank_homG_self` gives `≥ 1` for any nonzero representation; the content here is\n`≤ 1`, which is W2 — the commutant is the base field, so there is nothing beyond the scalars.\nMathlib obtains this normalisation only over an algebraically closed base\n(`FDRep.char_orthonormal`); no algebraic closure is used here.\n\n`-- Ref: [james1984representation] §4; [sagan2001] §2.4` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.homG_specht_self_eq_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.homG_specht_self_eq_span","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtSchurDiagonal.lean#L66-L78","doc":"**`Hom_G(S^μ, S^μ)` is the line through the identity.** The inclusion `⊇` is that the\nidentity is equivariant; `⊆` is W2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.id_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.id_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtSchurDiagonal.lean#L59-L64","doc":"The identity is a nonzero endomorphism of `S^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.nontrivial_spechtSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtSchurDiagonal.nontrivial_spechtSubmodule","kind":"instance","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtSchurDiagonal.lean#L49-L57","doc":"`S^μ` is nonzero: it contains a polytabloid, and polytabloids do not vanish in\ncharacteristic zero (`SpechtCrossKappa.polytabloid_ne_zero`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}